  "market_commentary": {
    "overview": "",
    "bulkers": "One more very busy s+p week with supramax sales dominating the deals, having recorded \nnine (9) units changing hands; we understand that ten (10) eager buyers competed for the Cebu built \n2013 Tess 58 named \"KN Future\" which was finally sold for the strong level of either $18.3 or $18.75 \nmill. One more Cebu 2011 built Tess 58 named \"Eternity SW\" went for the softer price of $15 mill to \nChinese interests. In a private transaction, Vietnamese splurged $17 mill for \"Super Saka\" (55k built \n2011 Mitsui/Japan).",
